  "worked_solution": "The modes of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that the global maxima of $f(x)$ are at $x=3,9.$\n\nTherefore, the modes of $X$ are $3$  and $9.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/4cc925bf2013c4af687cd917bd8550a4bce7b9f1d7ae0de404af36db567333a7.png)",
